    "result_text": "The full suite is a single test class (the rest are base/helper classes), and it passes. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe membership level is derived in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`). I changed it so that level 4 is gated on tenure:\n\n- The email (+1) and `namesakeCount == 0` (+1) factors on top of the base 1 now cap at **3** via `Math.min(level, 3)`.\n- A **4th** level is added only when tenure \u2014 days between `registrationDate` and today \u2014 is **more than 365 days** (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...) > 365`), then re-capped at 4.\n\nSince `BuildOwner` sets a new owner's `registrationDate` to the current (business) day, a newly created owner has zero tenure and therefore maxes out at level 3 \u2014 exactly as the new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts. I also added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import and updated the Javadoc to reflect the tenure gate.",
